    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-5" id="fn-5" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Steam</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-6" id="fn-6" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Cancelled Project Costs in IA 2016 Test Year Rate Review: Iowa Utilities Commission Order RPU-2017-0001 authorized a ten year amortization period starting May 2018 and ending April 2028.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-7" id="fn-7" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Iowa Electric &amp; Gas 2024-2025 Rate Revew Costs: Iowa Utilities Commission Order TF-2024-0098 authorized an amortization of electric rate case expenses starting September 2025 and ending October 2029. Iowa Utilities Commission Order TF-2024-0099 authorized an amortization of gas rate case expenses beginning September 2025 and ending January 2028.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-8" id="fn-8" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Coal Costs from Lansing Retirement: IUC order RPU-2023-0002 authorized a 13 year amortization period starting October 2024 and ending February 2037.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-9" id="fn-9" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Balance includes $56.8 million of investment tax credits.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-10" id="fn-10" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Tax Reform Regulatory Impacts: Iowa Utilities Commission Order RPU-2023-002 authorized IPL to utilize a portion of both the protected and unprotected excess accumulated deferred income taxes (ADIT) to offset rate impacts. FERC Order ER19-257-000 authorized IPL to utilize the excess ADIT benefits in the wholesale formula rate true-up process.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-11" id="fn-11" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Over Collection Plant Removal Costs: FERC Docket No. AC19-15-000 authorized classification of over collection of plant removal costs as a regulatory liability.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-12" id="fn-12" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Deferred Pension &amp; OPEB Costs: Iowa Utilities Commission Order RPU-2023-002 authorized deferral accounting treatment for the Pension and Other Post Employment Benefits costs.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-13" id="fn-13" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">2025 Electric Earnings Sharing Mechanism: Iowa Utilities Commission Order RPU-2023-0002 authorized IPL to apply excess earnings to the remaining net book value of IPL&#8217;s highest earning asset with advance ratemaking principles (currently the Emery Generation Station) based on its authorized return on common equity.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-14" id="fn-14" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Account 442 sales are classified as commercial or industrial based on the energy being consumed in facilities occupied for commercial or industrial purposes. Commercial facilities generally consist of service-producing businesses while industrial facilities are generally used for producing, processing, or assembling goods.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-15" id="fn-15" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">MISO Schedule 24 charges and MISO FERC assessment charges.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-16" id="fn-16" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">MISO FERC assessment charges.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-17" id="fn-17" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Transmission usage interconnection lease payments.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-18" id="fn-18" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Facilities Service Agreement fees for Beaver Creek-Grimes tie line, Burlington Generating Station, Creston Solar Farm, English Farms Wind Farm, Franklin County Wind Farm, Golden Plains Wind Farm, Marshalltown Generating Station, Pleasant Creek Unit 1 Solar Farm, Richland Wind Farm, Wever Solar Farm, Whispering Willow North Wind Farm, and Whispering Willow East Wind Farm.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-19" id="fn-19" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Represents the (under)/over collected transmission rider revenues from Iowa Jurisdiction customers in accordance with IUC Rate Orders.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-20" id="fn-20" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Transmission facility charges at jointly-owned plants operated by MidAmerican Energy Company and Facilities Service Agreement fees for Golden Plains Wind Farm and Beaver Creek-Grimes tie line.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-21" id="fn-21" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Facilities Service Agreement fees for City of Lester tie line.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-22" id="fn-22" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">FERC Account 561.1 includes $125,476 of costs incurred for transmission dispatching services, offset by ($125,476) billed to ITC Midwest LLC.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-23" id="fn-23" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">FERC Account 561.4 includes $169,218 of costs incurred related to Balancing Authority Functions performed in connection with membership in MISO. Also included are ($139,215) of cost recoveries from MISO of Balancing Authority function costs.</link:footnote>
